# HoA Digital Skills & Infrastructure Audit Form

Setup Guide for Microsoft Forms

## Quick Overview

This form collects comprehensive digital skills and infrastructure data from all 34 curriculum areas. HoAs fill it in themselves (15–20 mins) with the Digital Skills Framework as reference. Responses auto-populate a SharePoint list or downloadable Excel for your manual sync into the tracker.

## Step-by-Step Setup

- Open forms.office.com and sign in with your college account

- Click "New Form"

- Copy this title: "HoA Digital Skills & Infrastructure Audit"

- Copy this description: "Digital skills mapping and infrastructure assessment for your curriculum area. Uses the Weston College Digital Skills Framework as reference. Takes 15–20 minutes."

- Set to "Collaborators can edit form" (allows HoAs to revisit and update)

## Form Questions — Copy & Paste

### SECTION 1: RESPONDENT INFO

Q1: Your Curriculum Area

Type: Short answer | Required | Placeholder: "e.g. Engineering & Motor Vehicle [EMV]"

Q2: Your Name

Type: Short answer | Required

### SECTION 2: DIGITAL SKILLS FOR LEARNERS & STAFF

Add Section Break

Heading: "Section 1: Digital Skills for Your Learners & Staff"

Description: "Reference: Digital Skills Framework Tab 2 (All Subjects & Curriculum Areas) and Tab 3 (Industry-Specific Digital Skills)."

Q3: Core Digital Skills for Learners

Type: Long answer | Required

Instructions: "List 3–5 digital skills your learners MUST develop to succeed in your industry or next progression route. Include both general EDS skills (communication, data handling, AI literacy) and industry-specific tools (e.g. CAD, diagnostic software, clinical systems). Be as specific as possible."

Note: "Examples from the framework: Construction learners need CAD/BIM, digital site diaries, QR clock-in systems. Health learners need electronic patient records (SystmOne/EMIS), telehealth platforms. Creative learners need Adobe Suite, version control, AI-assisted design tools."

Q4: How Have These Skills Been Baselined?

Type: Long answer | Optional

Instructions: "How do you currently measure or track whether your learners are developing these skills? (e.g. entry diagnostic, end-of-unit assessment, placement feedback, employer feedback, portfolio evidence)"

Q5: Staff Digital Capability Needed

Type: Long answer | Required

Instructions: "What digital skills do YOUR STAFF need to teach these competently? (e.g. ability to use the industry-standard tools themselves, confidence with digital assessment, ability to troubleshoot learner digital problems, knowledge of AI in your sector)"

Q6: Staff Readiness — Current State

Type: Long answer | Optional

Instructions: "Where are your staff currently on the journey? Are they confident with these tools? Where are the gaps? (Reference: Framework Tab 7 — Teacher Digital Skills Progression)"

### SECTION 3: HARDWARE INFRASTRUCTURE

Add Section Break

Heading: "Section 2: Hardware Infrastructure"

Description: "Assess your current device access and what you need."

Q7: Devices — Current State

Type: Long answer | Required | Instructions: "What devices do your learners currently have access to in college? (e.g. college PCs, tablets, laptops, industry-specific equipment like diagnostic tools, VR headsets, 3D printers)"

Q8: Devices — What You Need

Type: Long answer | Optional | Instructions: "What devices or equipment would significantly improve your teaching and learner outcomes? What's missing or out of date?"

Q9: Network & Connectivity

Type: Long answer | Optional | Instructions: "Are there connectivity issues in your teaching spaces? (e.g. Wi-Fi strength, bandwidth, mobile signal, printing infrastructure)"

### SECTION 4: SOFTWARE & LEARNING TOOLS

Add Section Break

Heading: "Section 3: Software & Learning Tools"

Description: "Map your current software provision against what you need."

Q10: Software — Currently Available

Type: Long answer | Required | Instructions: "What software or digital tools do your learners currently have access to? (Include: VLE, Teams, Microsoft 365, industry-specific applications, simulation software, design tools, any sector-specific platforms)"

Q11: Software — Critical Gaps

Type: Long answer | Optional | Instructions: "What industry-standard tools are you NOT able to access right now but NEED? (e.g. CAD software, diagnostic platforms, design suites, data analysis tools). What would unlock better learning?"

Q12: VLE & Digital Learning Environment

Type: Long answer | Optional | Instructions: "How are you currently using your VLE (Moodle/Canvas)? Is it functioning well for your area? Any gaps in digital delivery infrastructure?"

### SECTION 5: ACCESSIBILITY & ASSISTIVE TECHNOLOGY

Add Section Break

Heading: "Section 4: Accessibility & Assistive Technology"

Description: "Assess your current support for learners with SEND and accessibility needs."

Q13: Assistive Technology — Currently Available

Type: Long answer | Optional | Instructions: "What assistive technology or accessibility tools do you currently have available for learners with SEND? (e.g. Read&Write, Immersive Reader, speech-to-text, eye-gaze software, switch access, adapted keyboards)"

Q14: Accessibility — Barriers for Learners

Type: Long answer | Optional | Instructions: "Are there learners in your area who cannot access digital resources or tools due to accessibility issues? What's blocking them? (Reference: Framework Tab 5 — SEND & Inclusion)"

### SECTION 6: BARRIERS & BLOCKERS

Add Section Break

Heading: "Section 5: Barriers & Blockers"

Description: "Be honest about what's preventing you from delivering industry-standard digital skills."

Q15–Q19: Barrier questions (Device Access, Software Licensing, Staff Capability, Network, Other)

Type: Long answer | Optional each

(See setup guide in outputs folder for full text of each — they follow the same pattern: "How does [barrier] hinder your teaching?")

### SECTION 7: IMPACT & EVIDENCE

Add Section Break

Heading: "Section 6: Impact & Evidence"

Description: "Tell us about the impact digital skills are having (or could have) on your learners."

Q20: Current Impact — What's Working?

Type: Long answer | Optional

Instructions: "What digital approaches or tools are currently having a positive impact on your learners? Can you give a concrete example? (e.g. employer feedback, progression rates, learner confidence, assessment outcomes)"

Q21: Potential Impact — If We Resolved the Barriers

Type: Long answer | Optional

Instructions: "If we removed the top barriers (better devices, staff CPD, software access), what difference would it make to your learners' outcomes?"

### SECTION 8: SUPPORT & NEXT STEPS

Add Section Break

Heading: "Section 7: Support & Next Steps"

Description: "What support would help most?"

Q22: What Support Would Help Most?

Type: Long answer | Optional

Q23: Anything Else?

Type: Long answer | Optional

## After Creating the Form

### 1. Add Hyperlinks to the Framework

In each section description, add clickable links to the Digital Skills Framework tabs. You can do this directly in Forms by pasting the link URL.

- Tab 2 (All Subjects): https://gwc25.github.io/Digital-Skills-Framework/#tab02

- Tab 3 (Industry-Specific): https://gwc25.github.io/Digital-Skills-Framework/#tab03

- Tab 5 (SEND & Inclusion): https://gwc25.github.io/Digital-Skills-Framework/#tab05

- Tab 7 (Teacher Skills): https://gwc25.github.io/Digital-Skills-Framework/#tab07

### 2. Share the Form

- Click "Share" in the top right, copy the link

- Send to all HoAs with a covering email (see template below)

- Set deadline (suggest end of Friday this week)

### 3. Collect & Review Responses

- In Forms, click "Responses" tab to see live responses

- Click "Open in Excel" to download all responses

- Manually sync key findings into your HoA tracker (barriers, skills gaps, infrastructure needs)

## Email Template to HoAs

Subject: Digital Skills & Infrastructure Audit — Please Complete by Friday

Hi [HoA Name],

As part of the Digital Leads Programme planning, we're running a digital skills and infrastructure audit across all 34 curriculum areas. This helps us understand what you need, what's working, and what barriers we need to tackle together.

Please fill in this form by end of day Friday. It takes 15–20 minutes. As you fill it in, you'll see prompts to reference the Digital Skills Framework — this gives you concrete examples of what we're asking for rather than generic questions.

[FORM LINK]

The form covers:

- Digital skills your learners and staff need

- Current hardware (devices)

- Software and learning tools you have access to

- Accessibility and assistive technology

- Real barriers preventing you from delivering digital skills (devices, licensing, staff, network, etc.)

- Impact you're already seeing from digital approaches

This is your honest input — we want to hear what's actually happening in your area, not what you think we want to hear. The barriers section especially: we need to know what's hindering you so we can do something about it.

Questions? Email me or catch me before Heads Together next Wednesday.

Graeme

## Troubleshooting

### HoAs can't edit/submit after initial submission

Make sure you turned on "Collaborators can edit form" when you created it.

### Links to the framework tabs don't work

Make sure the URLs have the correct anchor tags (#tab02, #tab03, etc.). Test them in a new browser tab before sharing the form.

### Excel download has empty rows

This is normal in Forms — it includes section breaks as rows. Just filter them out when syncing into your tracker.